From 7ac7598d393baac49bad01c3b332801bc5580397 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 09:55:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 84/98] docs: drop Xenix from the personality target list
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Microsoft Xenix and SCO Xenix are not on the near-term roadmap; remove them
from docs/specs/personality_targets.md.  (They were never in the kernel
personality enum or the README — this is the only place they appeared.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/specs/personality_targets.md | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/specs/personality_targets.md b/docs/specs/personality_targets.md
index 38a61ba5..7505597b 100644
--- a/docs/specs/personality_targets.md
+++ b/docs/specs/personality_targets.md
@@ -9,8 +9,6 @@ The following execution personalities are planned or implemented for Substrate:
 - **OpenBSD**
 - **Solaris / SVR4 family**
 - **SunOS 4.x (Sun386i)**
-- **Microsoft Xenix** (`MS-X/86`, `MS-X/286`, `MS-X/386`)
-- **SCO Xenix** (`SCO-X/86`, `SCO-X/286`, `SCO-X/386`)
 - **SCO Unix** (`SCO-U/3.2v2`, `SCO-U/ODT3`, `SCO-OSR5`)
 - **iBCS2** compatibility targets
 - **ELKS** (16-bit Linux-like)
-- 
2.54.0

